\f0\b\fs46 \cf2 ANTIHUNTER DIGI NODE\

\fs38 TIER 1 \'96 FULLY ASSEMBLED UNIT
\f1\b0\fs32 \cf0 \
\
Built, soldered and bench-tested. Meshtastic is flashed on the radio with the serial link to the node already configured.\
\
\

\f0\b IN THE BOX
\f1\b0 \
\

\f0\b Assembled node - 
\f1\b0 8 GB microSD fitted, TPU sealed\

\f0\b Active GPS helix antenna
\f1\b0  - Attach to center SMA\

\f0\b 2.4 GHz WiFi/BLE SMA antenna
\f1\b0  - Attach to left SMA\

\f0\b LoRa SMA antenna for your region
\f1\b0  (915 US) - Attach to right SMA\
\
You supply: two 18650 batteries: Flat top, same brand and capacity.\
\
\

\f0\b SET IT UP
\f1\b0 \
\
1. Remove back cover, fit the two batteries, correct orientation. A tiny red LED illumination on the UPS is expected when batteries are present.\
\
2. Screw on the antennas (Left: WiFI, Right: LoRa). Finger tight, then an eighth of a turn. Never power the node with the LoRa antenna missing.\
\
3. Flash AntiHunter on the ESP32 over USB. Web flasher: lukeswitz.github.io/AntiHunter. Pick Full for the web UI, or Headless for quiet field ops.\
\
4. Set the LoRa region on the radio. It ships UNSET, which means receive only, and the node will not answer over mesh until you set it.\
\
5. Change the Bluetooth pairing pin on the radio. Every unit ships with the same one. You can disable it and use a cable to manage the Heltec board for more silent operation. \
\
6. Make your own encrypted Meshtastic channel primary and turn the public default channel off.\
\
7. Full firmware: join the 
\f0\b Antihunter
\f1\b0  WiFi AP, password 
\f0\b antihunt3r123
\f1\b0 , open http://192.168.4.1 and change those credentials first.\
\
8. Add the USB seal for outdoor use. The included GPS antenna has a built in rubber seal, there is no need to use the included seal unless changing antennas.\
\

\f0\b POWER
\f1\b0 \
\
Regulated 5 V only, from USB or the UPS board. Never wire cells or an unregulated supply to the PCB. 
\f0\b One USB cable at a time.
\f1\b0 \
\
The fan is fitted blowing out and comes on when the thermal switch closes. Short the two THERMO pins to run it all the time.\
\
\

